.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH soundcraft-cli-run 1  "run " 
.SH NAME
soundcraft\-cli\-run \- Run engine commands on a new, demo or saved session
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsoundcraft\-cli run\fR [\fB\-\-cmd\fR] [\fB\-\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-bounce\fR] [\fB\-\-start\fR] [\fB\-\-end\fR] [\fB\-\-save\fR] [\fB\-\-inspect\fR] [\fB\-\-compact\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-place\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run engine commands on a new, demo or saved session
.PP
Prints each command\*(Aqs JSON result on one line, then bounces, saves and inspects, in that order. The \-\-inspect JSON is pretty\-printed unless \-\-compact is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-cmd\fR \fI<ID[=JSON]>\fR
An engine command, with its JSON parameters after `=` (default {}); repeat for several, run in order
.TP
\fB\-\-in\fR \fI<S.scraft>\fR
Open this session first
.TP
\fB\-\-demo\fR
Start from the demo session
.TP
\fB\-\-bounce\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Bounce the mix to this file at the end; without \-\-start and \-\-end, the whole session
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fI<T>\fR
Where the bounce starts: seconds (12.5) or a time string
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fI<T>\fR
Where the bounce ends: seconds (12.5) or a time string
.TP
\fB\-\-save\fR \fI<S.scraft>\fR
Save the session to this file at the end, replacing it
.TP
\fB\-\-inspect\fR
Print the session as JSON at the end
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\fR
Print the \-\-inspect JSON on one line instead of pretty\-printed
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
Allow a \-\-save that is the \-\-in session, replacing the original
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
